course: dictionary
lesson: 7940
title: Rearrange: change the order
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: To rearrange means to change the order or position of things. You keep the same things but put them in a new place or sequence. «We will rearrange the furniture so there is space to dance.» The sofa and the table are still there, just in new places.
explain: Rearrange can also mean to change the time or date of an event. «We'll rearrange the dentist appointment» means the visit will happen at a different time. The appointment is still happening; only its time has changed.
explain: In maths, rearranging changes the order of numbers or letters, or moves one letter so it stands alone in a formula. In a word puzzle, you rearrange the letters to make a new word. Check your answer by counting that you still have every letter.
fact: To rearrange means to change the order or position of things.
fact: An anagram is a word made by rearranging all the letters of another word: «listen» gives «silent», and «night» gives «thing».
fact: «The letters of CHIEN can be rearranged into NICHE», and «une niche» is a dog's kennel.
fact: When you rearrange things, you do not lose or add any: the same items are simply in a new order.
exercise: «We will rearrange the chairs before the party.» What does rearrange mean here? | Count the chairs | Break the chairs | *Change where the chairs are | Paint the chairs
exercise: «Can we rearrange our meeting to Friday?» What does rearrange mean? | Make the meeting longer | *Change the time or date | Cancel the meeting forever | Invite more people
exercise: Rearrange the letters of NIGHT to make a new word. Which word do you get? | happy | cloud | *thing | nights
test: In maths, what does it mean to rearrange a formula? | To rub out the whole formula | *To change it so a different letter is on its own | To copy it onto another page | To add a new number to the end of it
test: «No atom is lost in a reaction; the atoms are only rearranged.» What does rearranged mean here? | *Put into a new order or arrangement | Taken away and never seen | Destroyed completely | Counted again from the start
exam: Which word is made by rearranging all the letters of EARTH? | earthy | threat | *heart | hearth
